---
title: Corvidae
---
# Corvidae

Corvidae is the crow family, taking in the ravens, jays, magpies and nutcrackers.
Its members have the largest brains relative to body size of any birds, and
several species cache food in scattered sites and recover it months later. The
family is omnivorous and opportunistic, and many species are bold around human
settlement. See [[common-raven]].
